Subject: [PATCH] agent: refresh authoritative channels on a monotonic deadline

The initial publication latch only records local send success. Lost renews or
reports can leave controller inventory empty indefinitely. Refresh real native
channels without restarting services or synthesizing channel values.

Schedule refresh for 30 steady-clock seconds after successful publication.
The manager's nominal two-second callback alternates two/three seconds because
its demultiplexer resets every five seconds; fifteen callbacks take 37-38
seconds, not 30. Check the elapsed deadline at each existing callback, including
delayed handlers, rather than counting calls. Publication occurs on the first
scheduler opportunity at/after the deadline; this is not an instantaneous or
hard wall-clock delivery guarantee. Readiness and transport still matter.

Keep initial/renew retries and preserve the initial-success latch on failed
periodic refresh so the independent association snapshot gate stays enabled.
Extracted native manager scheduler tests cover 2/32/62-second publication,
failed refresh, delayed handlers, and catch-up without premature publication.

Upstream-Status: Pending

